IMPORT prelude

-- Smoking (Prohibition in Certain Places) Act 1992 (Singapore) -- what counts as "smoking" (s 2), where it is prohibited (ss 3,
-- 3A, 3B), smoking facilities and the Director-General's designation of them (ss 3C, 3D), arrest and entry (ss 4, 4A), obstruction
-- (s 4B), the duties of managers and operators (ss 5, 6), and composition (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/5/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SPCPA1992.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 9 of 2026 wef 01/05/2026 (the vaporiser carve-out in the definition of "smoking"). THE ARRANGEMENT
-- OF SECTIONS AT THE TOP OF THE DEPOSIT IS ONE ROW OUT OF STEP WITH THE BODY (it lists "3A. No smoking in specified places",
-- "4. Appeal to Minister" and so on). This encoding follows the section numbers in the BODY: s 3 is the prohibition, s 3A
-- specified places, s 3B exceptions, s 3C smoking facilities, s 3D appeals, s 4 arrest, s 4A entry, s 4B obstruction, s 5 notices,
-- s 6 duties of managers, s 7 composition.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the law that decides where a person in Singapore may light a
-- cigarette, what a coffee-shop or condominium manager must do about someone who does, and what the fine is. SCOPED to the rules a
-- smoker, a bystander, or a manager of a place meets. Not encoded: which places and vehicles have actually been prescribed (that
-- is done by regulations, none of which was retrieved), the "prescribed circumstances" in s 3B, the prescribed requirements for
-- smoking facilities, the prescribed appeal period (s 3D(2)(c)), the list of compoundable offences, s 4A(1) inspection powers
-- beyond entry, s 4A(4) statements, s 8 (where fees go), ss 9-12 (forms, exemption orders, regulations, transition) beyond the
-- bare effect of an exemption.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Smoking (Prohibition in Certain Places) Act 1992`

§§ `2 -- what counts as smoking`

-- s 2 "smoking" (a) "means inhaling and expelling the smoke of tobacco or any other substance, and includes the holding of any cigar,
-- cigarette or pipe or any other form of tobacco product that is alight or emitting smoke; but (b) does not include inhaling and
-- expelling the smoke emitted by a vaporiser ... or the holding of any vaporiser that is emitting smoke" [Act 9 of 2026 wef
-- 01/05/2026].
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `puffing a lit cigarette`
    `holding a lit cigarette without puffing`
    `holding a lit cigar`
    `holding a smouldering pipe`
    `holding an unlit cigarette`
    `smoking shisha`
    `inhaling and expelling the smoke of a non-tobacco herbal roll`
    `using a vaporiser`
    `holding a vaporiser emitting smoke`
    `chewing tobacco`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is smoking` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `puffing a lit cigarette` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `holding a lit cigarette without puffing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `holding a lit cigar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `holding a smouldering pipe` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `smoking shisha` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `inhaling and expelling the smoke of a non-tobacco herbal roll` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3A -- specified places and no-smoking zones`

-- s 2 "place" means any premises, structure or building, "or any unenclosed area (including a road, pavement, wetland and any body
-- of water), but not a vehicle". "publicly accessible place": the public or a section of it has access "as of right, or by virtue of
-- express or implied permission with or without payment of a fee".
-- s 3A(1): the Agency may, with the Minister's approval, prescribe as a specified place (a) any publicly accessible place; (b) any of
-- the following that is NOT publicly accessible: (i) a place owned, managed or occupied by the Government or a statutory body;
-- (ii) "any common property of any residential premises or building"; (iii) a commercial or industrial place (or mixed, predominantly
-- so) or its common property; (iv) any recreational facility; (c) a passenger ship, boat, air-cushioned vehicle or similar craft.
-- s 3A(3): every publicly accessible place within a no-smoking zone, not otherwise prescribed, "is a specified place from the date
-- the area is prescribed as a no-smoking zone".
--
-- A flat or house that is not common property, not publicly accessible, not Government-run and not commercial falls in none of the
-- heads, so the Act gives no power to prescribe it.
DECLARE Place HAS
    `is publicly accessible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is Government or statutory body premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is residential common property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is commercial or industrial premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a recreational facility` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a passenger vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been prescribed as a specified place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lies in a prescribed no-smoking zone` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is capable of being prescribed` IF
        `the place`'s `is publicly accessible`
    OR  `the place`'s `is Government or statutory body premises`
    OR  `the place`'s `is residential common property`
    OR  `the place`'s `is commercial or industrial premises`
    OR  `the place`'s `is a recreational facility`
    OR  `the place`'s `is a passenger vessel`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is a specified place` IF
        (`the place`'s `has been prescribed as a specified place` AND `the place is capable of being prescribed` `the place`)
    OR  (`the place`'s `is publicly accessible` AND `the place`'s `lies in a prescribed no-smoking zone`)

§§ `3, 3B, 10 -- the prohibition and its exceptions`

-- s 3(1): "Subject to section 3B, a person must not smoke in a specified place or specified vehicle." (2): fine not exceeding $1,000.
-- s 3B(1): smoking in a specified place is permitted only (a) "when within a smoking facility in the specified place"; or (b) in
-- prescribed circumstances. (2): in a specified vehicle, ONLY in prescribed circumstances -- there is no smoking facility in a vehicle.
-- s 2 "specified vehicle" is a PUBLIC SERVICE VEHICLE prescribed under s 3A(4). A private car is neither a "place" nor a "specified
-- vehicle", so the Act cannot reach it.
-- s 10: the Agency may by order in the Gazette exempt "any person or place from all or any of the provisions of this Act".
DECLARE Situation HAS
    `what the person is doing` IS AN Activity
    `is in a specified place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a specified vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is within a smoking facility` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed circumstances apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exemption order covers it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the situation` IS A Situation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `smoking here is permitted by section 3B` IF
        (`the situation`'s `is in a specified place` AND `the situation`'s `is within a smoking facility`)
    OR  `the situation`'s `prescribed circumstances apply`

GIVEN `the situation` IS A Situation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the section 3 offence` IF
        `the activity is smoking` (`the situation`'s `what the person is doing`)
    AND (`the situation`'s `is in a specified place` OR `the situation`'s `is in a specified vehicle`)
    AND (NOT `smoking here is permitted by section 3B` `the situation`)
    AND (NOT `the situation`'s `an exemption order covers it`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for smoking in a specified place` MEANS 1000

§§ `3C -- smoking facilities`

-- s 3C(3): the manager, or the Director-General, may designate an area or room as a smoking facility, but only in a specified place
-- prescribed as one in which a smoking facility may be located. (5): the manager must ensure every smoking facility complies with
-- the prescribed requirements. (6): (a) fine not exceeding $5,000 and, for a continuing offence, a further $500 "for every day or
-- part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction"; (b) second or subsequent conviction: $10,000 or 3 months or
-- both, and the same $500 a day. (7): defence if "it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact done" or "there
-- was no better practicable means than what was in fact used".
GIVEN `the facility complies` IS A BOOLEAN, `not reasonably practicable to do more` IS A BOOLEAN, `no better practicable means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager is guilty over the smoking facility` IF
        (NOT `the facility complies`)
    AND (NOT `not reasonably practicable to do more`)
    AND (NOT `no better practicable means`)

GIVEN `a previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a non-compliant smoking facility` MEANS
    IF `a previous conviction`
    THEN 10000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continued after conviction`
    ELSE 5000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `a previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for a non-compliant smoking facility` MEANS
    IF `a previous conviction` THEN 3 ELSE 0

§§ `3C(4), 3D -- the Director-General's designation and the appeal`

-- s 3C(4): before designating, the Director-General must (a) give the manager written notice of the intention "and when the
-- designation is to take effect"; and (b) give the manager an opportunity to submit reasons within the period in the notice.
-- s 3D(2): an appeal must (a) be in writing; (b) specify the grounds; (c) be made within the prescribed period after receipt of the
-- notice. (3): the Minister "may reject" a non-complying appeal. (5): the decision is final. (7): a designation appealed against "does
-- not take effect until the appeal is determined or earlier withdrawn".
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `states grounds` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may reject the appeal as non-compliant` IF
    NOT (`in writing` AND `states grounds` AND `within the prescribed period`)

GIVEN `notice and opportunity were given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the notified date has arrived` IS A BOOLEAN, `an appeal was made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the appeal was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal was determined` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal was allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General's designation has taken effect` IF
        `notice and opportunity were given`
    AND `the notified date has arrived`
    AND (    (NOT `an appeal was made`)
         OR  `the appeal was withdrawn`
         OR  (`the appeal was determined` AND (NOT `the appeal was allowed`)))

§§ `4 -- arrest and notice to attend court`

-- s 4(1): anyone reasonably suspected of an offence under this Act "may be arrested without warrant by any police officer or
-- authorised officer". (2): an officer "satisfied as to the identity, name and place of residence" of the person may, instead of
-- producing the person before a court, serve a notice to attend court. (6): failure to attend -- the court may issue a warrant.
GIVEN `arrested` IS A BOOLEAN, `identity known` IS A BOOLEAN, `name known` IS A BOOLEAN, `residence known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may serve a notice to attend court instead` IF
    `arrested` AND `identity known` AND `name known` AND `residence known`

§§ `4A(2), (3) -- entry without a warrant`

-- s 4A(2): entry may be made (a) "in relation to a specified place that is common property of any residential premises or building
-- which is not a publicly accessible place -- ONLY if the condition mentioned in subsection (3) is satisfied"; (b) elsewhere (i) "at
-- all reasonable times" or (ii) at any time if the condition is satisfied. (3): the officer reasonably believes an offence has been
-- or is being committed there, or evidence of one can be found there.
GIVEN `private residential common property` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable belief of offence or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter without a warrant` IF
    IF `private residential common property`
    THEN `reasonable belief of offence or evidence`
    ELSE `at a reasonable time` OR `reasonable belief of offence or evidence`

§§ `4B -- obstruction`

-- s 4B(1): an offence, "without reasonable excuse", to (a) obstruct, hinder or delay; (b) neglect or refuse to produce or provide;
-- (c) produce or provide anything "false or misleading in any material particular"; (d) neglect or refuse to attend. Fine not
-- exceeding $2,000; second or subsequent OFFENCE, $5,000 or 3 months or both.
-- (2): "To avoid doubt, for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) or (b), it is a reasonable excuse" to refuse if doing so "might tend to
-- incriminate that person". The encoding confines the self-incrimination excuse to (a) and (b), as the text does; whether a court
-- would find it a reasonable excuse under (c) or (d) as well is not decided by the text (inference).
DECLARE Obstruction IS ONE OF
    `obstructing an officer`
    `refusing to produce a document or information`
    `giving false or misleading information`
    `refusing to attend`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS AN Obstruction, `some other reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `answering might incriminate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an obstruction offence` IF
        (NOT `some other reasonable excuse`)
    AND CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN NOT `answering might incriminate`
        WHEN `refusing to produce a document or information` THEN NOT `answering might incriminate`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `a previous offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstruction` MEANS IF `a previous offence` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000

§§ `5 -- no-smoking notices`

-- s 5(1): the manager of every specified place and the operator of every specified vehicle must (a) display "a suitable and
-- sufficient number of notices of adequate size or sizes in conspicuous positions" stating that smoking is prohibited by law; and
-- (b) comply with any direction of the Director-General about them. (3): fine not exceeding $1,000.
GIVEN `adequate notices displayed` IS A BOOLEAN, `a direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the direction was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager commits the notices offence` IF
        (NOT `adequate notices displayed`)
    OR  (`a direction was given` AND (NOT `the direction was complied with`))

§§ `6 -- what a manager must do about a smoker`

-- s 6(1): the manager or operator must (a) tell anyone smoking in contravention of s 3(1) "to cease smoking immediately, indicating
-- the penalty"; (b) if the person does not, ask the person to leave immediately. (2): if the person refuses to leave or to cease,
-- (a) seek the assistance of a police officer or authorised officer; (b) render reasonable assistance.
-- (3): anyone may complain to the manager, who must (a) take all reasonable steps to investigate; (b) if the complaint is true, act
-- under (1) or (2).
-- (4): offence for a manager or operator who fails to comply with (1) or (2) "in relation to any person whom the manager or operator
-- knows or ought reasonably to know is smoking", or with (3) in relation to a complaint. Fine not exceeding $1,000; second or
-- subsequent CONVICTION $2,000.
-- (5): the manager is "presumed, until the contrary is proved," to know where an employee under the manager's charge or supervision,
-- employed at the place, knows.
-- (7): a manager or operator is not liable to refund an admission fee or fare to a person told to leave under (1).
DECLARE Encounter HAS
    `the manager knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a supervised employee knew` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the manager proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `told the smoker to stop and of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the smoker stopped` IS A BOOLEAN
    `asked the smoker to leave` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the smoker left` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sought police or officer help` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the encounter` IS AN Encounter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager is fixed with knowledge` IF
        `the encounter`'s `the manager knew or ought to have known`
    OR  (`the encounter`'s `a supervised employee knew` AND (NOT `the encounter`'s `the manager proved lack of knowledge`))

GIVEN `the encounter` IS AN Encounter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager did what section 6 requires` IF
        `the encounter`'s `told the smoker to stop and of the penalty`
    AND (    `the encounter`'s `the smoker stopped`
         OR  (    `the encounter`'s `asked the smoker to leave`
              AND (`the encounter`'s `the smoker left` OR `the encounter`'s `sought police or officer help`)))

GIVEN `the encounter` IS AN Encounter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager commits the section 6 offence` IF
        `the manager is fixed with knowledge` `the encounter`
    AND (NOT `the manager did what section 6 requires` `the encounter`)

GIVEN `a complaint was received` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable steps to investigate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the complaint was true` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted against the smoker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager fails the complaint duty` IF
        `a complaint was received`
    AND (    (NOT `reasonable steps to investigate`)
         OR  (`the complaint was true` AND (NOT `acted against the smoker`)))

GIVEN `a previous conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a manager's section 6 failure` MEANS IF `a previous conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000

-- s 6(6): anyone who "hinders, obstructs, threatens, abuses, molests or assaults any manager or operator" in the performance of these
-- duties: fine not exceeding $1,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 MONTHS or both -- a longer term than any other offence in the Act.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for abusing a manager` MEANS 6

§§ `7 -- composition`

-- s 7(1): the Director-General may compound any offence "that is prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not
-- exceeding $500". (2): on payment, no further proceedings. s 8(2): composition sums go into the Consolidated Fund.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for that sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum offered` AT MOST 500
